{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[0,1],"question":"What accuracy did the industry-detection system achieve, and how many industry classes were in the taxonomy?","answer":"The system achieved 64.3% accuracy in detecting a user's industry, evaluated across a taxonomy of fourteen industry classes."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[2],"question":"How many blog users were included in the industry-annotated dataset built for this study?","answer":"Over 20,000 blog users."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What user metadata fields were linked to the blog users in the dataset besides their posted text?","answer":"Gender, location, occupation, introduction, and interests."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[4,5],"question":"At what geographic granularity did Hecht et al. and Han et al. each predict Twitter users' locations?","answer":"Hecht et al. predicted locations at nationwide and state levels using machine learning, while Han et al. used location indicative words to predict locations down to the city level."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[7],"question":"How many occupational classes did Huang et al. use to classify Sina Weibo users?","answer":"Twelve platform-defined occupational classes."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[8],"question":"Did the frequency of emotionally charged words in an industry correlate with that industry's gender dominance ratio?","answer":"No, the study found these frequencies did not statistically significantly correlate with an industry's gender dominance ratio, for either gender."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0112","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What kind of life events did Li et al.'s model aim to identify from social media users?","answer":"Major life events such as getting married, moving to a new place, or graduating."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"The proposed architecture shows improvements of up to two percentage points F β=1 for Chunking compared to a plausible baseline.","source_span":"The architecture shows improvements of up to two percentage points F β=1 for Chunking compared to a plausible baseline."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"The paper examines a hierarchy of POS tagging, Chunking, and Language Modeling tasks.","source_span":"This paper seeks to examine the POS tagging, Chunking and Language Modeling hierarchy"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"Language Modeling is treated as an auxiliary unsupervised task, so results are not presented for it.","source_span":"we consider Language Modeling as auxiliary - designed to improve performance on POS and Chunking, and so therefore results are not presented for this task"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"The network is a Bi-Directional Recurrent Neural Network (Bi-RNN) using Gated Recurrent Units (GRUs).","source_span":"Our network is a Bi-Directional Recurrent Neural Network (Bi-RNN) (schuster1997bidirectional) with Gated Recurrent Units (GRUs)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"The model has 3 sources of error signals, one for each task.","source_span":"Our model has 3 sources of error signals - one for each task."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"The neural network has one hidden layer, after which each successive task is supervised on the next layer.","source_span":"Our neural network has one hidden layer, after which each successive task is supervised on the next layer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"Skip connections are added from the hidden layer to the senior supervised layers to allow layers to ignore information from junior tasks.","source_span":"we add skip connections from the hidden layer to the senior supervised layers to allow layers to ignore information from junior tasks"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","statement":"According to abney1991parsing, Noun Phrase Chunking is a three-phase process: assign POS tags, group words into chunks, then build a parse tree.","source_span":"first, you read the words and assign a Part of Speech tag, you then use a 'Chunker' to group these words together into chunks depending on the context and the Parts of Speech, and finally you build a parse tree on top of the chunks"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[0],"question":"By how much did the proposed architecture improve Chunking performance compared to the baseline?","answer":"Up to two percentage points in F β=1 score for Chunking."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What three tasks make up the linguistically motivated hierarchy examined in this paper?","answer":"Part of Speech (POS) tagging, Chunking, and Language Modeling."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Why are results not presented for the Language Modeling task in this paper?","answer":"Because Language Modeling is treated as an auxiliary unsupervised task meant to improve performance on POS and Chunking, rather than being evaluated on its own."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What type of recurrent unit does the network use, and what overall RNN architecture is it?","answer":"It is a Bi-Directional Recurrent Neural Network (Bi-RNN) built with Gated Recurrent Units (GRUs)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[4],"question":"How many sources of error signal does the model have, and how are they distributed?","answer":"The model has 3 sources of error signals, one for each of the three tasks."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What is the purpose of the skip connections added from the hidden layer to the senior supervised layers?","answer":"They allow the senior layers to ignore information from junior tasks when their representations or predictions are inconsistent."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0113","fact_refs":[7],"question":"According to the original chunking paper referenced, what are the three phases of the Noun Phrase Chunking process?","answer":"First assign Part of Speech tags to the words, then group the words into chunks using a 'Chunker' based on context and POS tags, and finally build a parse tree on top of the chunks."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"The proposed framework is a Self-Taught Convolutional neural network framework for Short Text Clustering, dubbed STC^2.","source_span":"we propose a flexible Self-Taught Convolutional neural network framework for Short Text Clustering (dubbed STC^2)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"The proposed framework was tested on three public short text datasets and outperformed several popular clustering methods.","source_span":"outperform several popular clustering methods when tested on three public short text datasets"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"The K-means algorithm is used to obtain optimal clusters from the learned deep feature representations.","source_span":"we get the optimal clusters by employing K-means to cluster the learned representations"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"Yin and Wang proposed a Dirichlet multinomial mixture model-based approach for short text clustering.","source_span":"Yin and Wang BIBREF5 proposed a Dirichlet multinomial mixture model-based approach for short text clustering"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"Banerjee et al. improved the accuracy of short text clustering by enriching representation with additional features from Wikipedia.","source_span":"Banerjee et al. BIBREF3 proposed a method of improving the accuracy of short text clustering by enriching their representation with additional features from Wikipedia"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"Fodeh et al. incorporated semantic knowledge from an ontology into text clustering.","source_span":"Fodeh et al. BIBREF4 incorporate semantic knowledge from an ontology into text clustering"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"The paper uses a new short text dataset called Biomedical, not used in the earlier conference version of this work.","source_span":"we use a new short text dataset, Biomedical, in the experiment to verify the effectiveness of our approach"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"This paper is an extension of the authors' earlier conference paper (BIBREF16).","source_span":"This work is an extension of our conference paper BIBREF16"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","statement":"The datasets and software used in the experiments are made publicly available at the authors' website for reproducibility.","source_span":"we make the datasets and software used in our experiments publicly available at the website"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What does the abbreviation STC^2 stand for in this paper?","answer":"A Self-Taught Convolutional neural network framework for Short Text Clustering."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","fact_refs":[1],"question":"How many public short text datasets were used to test the proposed STC^2 framework?","answer":"Three public short text datasets."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What algorithm is used to obtain the final clusters after learning deep feature representations in STC^2?","answer":"The K-means algorithm."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What approach did Yin and Wang propose for short text clustering?","answer":"A Dirichlet multinomial mixture model-based approach."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What new dataset was introduced in this paper compared to its earlier conference version?","answer":"A new short text dataset called Biomedical, used to verify the effectiveness of the approach."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0114","fact_refs":[4,5],"question":"How did Banerjee et al. and Fodeh et al. each try to address the sparseness problem in short text clustering?","answer":"Banerjee et al. enriched text representation with additional features from Wikipedia, while Fodeh et al. incorporated semantic knowledge from an ontology into text clustering."}
